The question asks whether a relative class name (without a leading backslash) in `new` is resolved from the global root.

In PHP, when you use a relative class name (without a leading `\`) inside a namespace, it is resolved relative to the current namespace, NOT from the global root.

For example:
```php
namespace Foo;

class Bar {}

namespace Baz {
    new Foo\Bar(); // resolves to Foo\Bar (global)
    new Bar();      // resolves to Baz\Bar (current namespace), NOT \Bar
}
```

So the statement "relative class name in `new` is resolved from the global root" is FALSE. It's resolved from the current namespace.

The answer is "нет".

